# Secrets and server data: never commit
#
# On the server, config and secrets live in 1radioe-private/ next to the
# checkout. A local copy inside the checkout (for development) stays out
# of git with everything in it: config.php, webhook-secret, deploy log,
# inbox/, tmp/. The template is config.sample.php in the repo root.
1radioe-private/

# Generic secret material, wherever it ends up
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*deploy_key*
webhook-secret

# Database dumps contain station data, the admin password hash and the
# TOTP secret
*.sql
*.sql.gz

# Uploaded content: never commit
#
# Uploads stay untracked on purpose. The deploy runs `git reset --hard`,
# which leaves untracked files alone. If anything under media/ were ever
# committed, a deploy could overwrite uploads. Never use `git clean`.
www/media/
1radioe-media/

# Purchased music must never be published
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.aac
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.wav

# Local working files
#
# Design sources (Affinity) and drafts are kept locally only. Assets the
# app actually serves get exported into its asset folders and committed
# there. The handover is internal project planning, not part of the repo.
design/
HANDOVER.md

# Release archives (releases are git tags)
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Logs
*.log

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Claude Code and other AI tooling, local only
#
# Approved shell commands are stored as permission rules in
# .claude/settings*.json, verbatim, including any token or password that
# was part of the command. The global gitignore does not travel with the
# repo, so the whole folder is excluded here. Project MCP configs can hold
# API keys in their env blocks. CLAUDE.md itself may be committed, but
# must never contain secrets.
.claude/
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.local.md
